 "docs_billing_excerpt": {
  "type": "text",
  "record_type": "documentation",
  "url": "https://docs.cfo.ai/workspace-settings/billing",
  "title": "Billing and plan",
  "context": "## Plans\n\nOpen **Settings \u2192 Billing** to see the plans and switch between them. The plan cards show the current prices and limits for your workspace; the shape of each plan is:\n\n* **Free** \u2014 start with your own data. It comes with a one-time allotment of AI credits that does not replenish, accepts CSV uploads as the only data source, and needs no card.\n* **Starter** \u2014 build and run the finance model. Standard AI usage that resets monthly, five standard integrations, a ceiling on synced rows, the MCP server and Slack app, proactive alerts and Triggers, unlimited Models and Scenarios, and one dedicated workspace.\n* **Growth** \u2014 everything in Starter with a multiple of the AI usage, more integrations, and a higher synced-row ceiling.\n* **Enterprise** \u2014 custom pricing and AI credits. Adds premium integrations, including NetSuite and data warehouses, multiple workspaces, SSO / SAML, priority support, and a dedicated Forward Deployed Finance Partner with a shared Slack channel. The card opens a conversation with sales rather than switching the plan.\n\nIf your card is declined when you add it or pay, the form repeats the card provider's reason and adds **Check your payment details or try a different card.**\n\nUse the **Monthly** / **Annual** toggle to compare cadences. Annual is selected by default when you first choose a paid plan and shows the saving against monthly billing. A paid plan starts with a 14-day free trial: select **Start free trial** on the card. Nothing is charged when the trial starts, and the card shows the price that applies per month after the trial. When you sign up, the plan page says **\\$0 today. Cancel anytime before it ends and you won\u2019t be charged, and you still get all 14 days free.** The **Add a payment method** dialog names the date to cancel by. Canceling during the trial does not cut it short.\n\nPlans differ in how many connections of each class you can hold, not in what a connection does. File uploads never count toward the integration limit, and neither do the API and MCP connections Ari calls live; see [API and MCP connections do not sync](/integrations/integrations-directory#api-and-mcp-connections-do-not-sync).",
  "target": "workspace-settings/billing",
  "content_scope": "excerpt"
 }
